.com/1095123 Commit-Ready: Cheng-Han Yang &lt;chenghan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Cheng-Han Yang &lt;chenghan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1095123" owner_email="chenghan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/23/1095123/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I990bf6d82f69b42a711527ae878d11d0c24c2bc3" commit="bc28a60759316242c3a2942d1a280e8e27b2b38f" commit_message="tast-tests: Print found targets when NewConnForTarget() times out.  Actually, the typical way to find out the value to pass to NewConnForTarget() is to look at logs and pick an appropriate one.  BUG=None TEST=tast -verbose run betty-DUT arc.IntentForward  Change-Id: I990bf6d82f69b42a711527ae878d11d0c24c2bc3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1095060 Commit-Ready: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1095060" owner_email="nya@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/tast-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/tast-tests" ref="refs/changes/60/1095060/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I3c7e79758a48e3a47465c952549bb86d72632374" commit="ca1a25f41e5ded97bfc29cd1caa5696e51db11b2" commit_message="UPSTREAM: x86/entry/32: Add an ASM_CLAC to entry_SYSENTER_32  Both before and after 5f310f739b4c (&quot;x86/entry/32: Re-implement SYSENTER using the new C path&quot;), we relied on a uaccess very early in the SYSENTER path to clear AC.  After that change, though, we can potentially make it all the way into C code with AC set, which enlarges the attack surface for SMAP bypass by doing SYSENTER with AC set.  Strengthen the SMAP protection by addding the missing ASM_CLAC right at the beginning.  BUG=chromium:836330 TEST=Build and boot  Change-Id: I3c7e79758a48e3a47465c952549bb86d72632374 Signed-off-by: Andy Lutomirski &lt;luto@kernel.org&gt; Cc: Andy Lutomirski &lt;luto@amacapital.net&gt; Cc: Borislav Petkov &lt;bp@alien8.de&gt; Cc: Brian Gerst &lt;brgerst@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Denys Vlasenko &lt;dvlasenk@redhat.com&gt; Cc: H. Peter Anvin &lt;hpa@zytor.com&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Cc: Peter Zijlstra &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/3e36be110724896e32a4a1fe73bacb349d3cba94.1456262295.git.luto@kernel.org Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 04d1d281dcfe683a53cddfab8371fc8bb302b069) Signed-off-by: Zubin Mithra &lt;zsm@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1077202 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1077202" owner_email="zsm@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/02/1077202/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I980f78e4363ac01dae0f9fd2acd9cc9129859c8c" commit="9f550bcaf33aff0a443fc865bd56ae16e627926f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Mark rt5682 codec driver as BROKEN  The commit introducing the driver states &quot;TEST=With the whole series merged, verify audio on headset&quot;. Unfortunately, someone did not care about bisectability, resulting in a large number of compile errors when trying to build the driver. Mark it as BROKEN.  BUG=b:77943310 TEST=Build any allmodconfig target  Change-Id: I980f78e4363ac01dae0f9fd2acd9cc9129859c8c Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.g